From: MiniBandit <194791386+MiniBandit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 13:28:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Show the title's picture with its UI blended on top

The title presents two planes: its 3D picture, and a 4K plane with the UI
that the console draws over it. With neither setting, the larger plane is
shown, so the window showed the UI alone and stayed black through the
opening cutscene, behind the subtitles, while the frames held thousands
of draws. play-main-mac.sh now defaults to plane 0 with the UI blended
over it (VICTORY_PRESENT_PLANE=0, VICTORY_PRESENT_COMPOSITE=1), as the
November 27 controls trial set by hand. A setting exported first still
wins.
---
 tools/macos/play-main-mac.sh | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/macos/play-main-mac.sh b/tools/macos/play-main-mac.sh
index f7b5a28..9ae9698 100755
--- a/tools/macos/play-main-mac.sh
+++ b/tools/macos/play-main-mac.sh
@@ -40,6 +40,11 @@ d VICTORY_DESCRIPTOR_AS_DATA 1
 # Measured Nov 27, world frames per 120 s: 18 -> ~265, 4 -> 363/497, 6 -> 522/508/508, 8 -> 482/514/474/509;
 # p95 2 s -> 0.3-0.4 s. 6 grows swap least (+90-350 MB vs +400-1100 MB at 8).
 d VICTORY_DSTORAGE_WORKERS 6
+# The title presents two planes: its 3D picture, and a 4K plane with the UI
+# that the console draws over it. Show plane 0, the picture, with the UI
+# blended on top. Otherwise the larger plane, the UI alone, is shown, and
+# cutscenes and much of the world are black behind the subtitles and HUD.
+d VICTORY_PRESENT_PLANE 0;        d VICTORY_PRESENT_COMPOSITE 1
 # Presses Enter on the first screens (20, 30 and 40 s in). Set VICTORY_KEYS= to turn it off.
 d VICTORY_KEYS 20:Enter,30:Enter,40:Enter
 # Faster, lower resolution: VICTORY_OUTPUT=1920x1080
